      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day, and usually 2,400 mg/day or less). That much raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nSome common regimens you might have meant:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common upper-range anti-inflammatory dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the absolute maximum\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is what you meant. If it is, I'd suggest a second check first. Once I have the details, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
