       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg per dose and 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. Higher doses don't give more pain relief or anti-inflammatory effect, but they do raise the risk of serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nHere are some other ways to go ahead:\n- **Enter a dose within range yourself.** The highest standard option is 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can enter that, or a lower dose such as 800 mg three times daily, right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending.** If you think this patient needs something unusual, a pharmacist or attending can review it. They can also enter an override through the hospital's own process.\n- **Consider other options.** If 3,200 mg/day isn't controlling the pain or inflammation, I can enter a scheduled acetaminophen order or another adjunct.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter the order."
